The attached image illustrates the anti-rPA IgG antibody titers in mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) alone or formulated with different doses of aluminum hydroxide (AH) or Nano-11. It demonstrates that both AH and Nano-11 significantly enhance the antibody response compared to rPA alone. Nano-11 at doses of 200 µg and 50 µg induces antibody titers comparable to or exceeding those achieved with AH at similar concentrations. Even at 12.5 µg, Nano-11 shows a significant adjuvant effect, indicating its efficacy in boosting humoral immunity.